/* ============================================================================
   ANJUM WEBS POS — MASTER DEVELOPER DASHBOARD (standalone, separate from the client app)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   This is a completely separate HTML file from shop-erp-cloud.html — it is never given to a
   shop/client, so nothing in here is discoverable via that file's view-source, and no client
   install has a code path, password prompt, or console command that can reach anything below.
   Keep this file on your own machine only.

   It talks to the SAME shared Firebase project every client build points at by default
   (FIREBASE_BUILTIN_CONFIG below must match the one in shop-erp-cloud.html). Three Firestore
   collections under system/license_registry drive everything:
     - "clients"      the master roster you manage here: credentials, locked Business Type,
                       plan tier, expiry, block status, per-client feature overrides.
     - "activations"  the live record a shop's own app reads/writes when it checks in. Every
                       write you make to a "clients" doc here also mirrors the fields that
                       matter (isPremium, businessType, businessTypeLocked, blocked, expiresAt,
                       featureOverrides) into the matching "activations" doc, so changes reach
                       the shop the next time their app is online — instantly if they have Cloud
                       Sync connected. A shop can also exist in "activations" without a "clients"
                       doc if they self-activated a generated key without being onboarded here;
                       those show up under "Unregistered Activations" so you can adopt them.
     - "audit_log"    a running record of actions taken from this dashboard (key generated,
                       client created, plan changed, suspended, etc.) for the Activity Log tab.
   There is also a top-level "system/feature_flags" document holding the global Free vs. Paid
   feature switchboard.

   IMPORTANT SCOPE NOTE: this file defines and writes all of the schema above. Whether
   shop-erp-cloud.html actually reads and enforces businessTypeLocked, blocked, tier, or
   featureOverrides depends on code in THAT file, which isn't part of this one — the original
   version of this dashboard already read/wrote isPremium and businessType that way, and the
   fields added here (blocked, tier, featureOverrides) follow the identical mirror pattern, but
   the client app needs its own matching read logic for each field to actually act on it.

   Login is a single password, compared only as a SHA-256 hash (never stored/shown in plaintext).
   CHANGE THE DEFAULT PASSWORD before relying on this — see CHANGING THE PASSWORD below.
   ============================================================================ */

